  "worked_solution": "The picture shows an *octahedron*, a convex regular polyhedron that  \n\n- consists of $8$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle, and\n\n- exactly $4$ faces meet at each vertex.\n\nRecall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)",
